# cl-stack conditions & restarts

First-party cl-stack only (`*-protocol`, `*-backend-*`, `cl-stack-*`). Not third-party forks.

The language is [CLHS 9](http://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/09_.htm). Do not invent a second error dialect.

- **Three parts** (PCL ch.19): signal at detection; restarts at the lowest site that can recover; policy in `handler-bind` above.
- **Standard names first:** `abort`, `continue`, `muffle-warning`, `store-value`, `use-value` — invoke via the [CLHS functions](http://clhs.lisp.se/Body/f_abortc.htm), not a private `invoke-*` unless the name is not standard (`retry` = ASDF convention → `invoke-restart`).
- **Domain restart** (`create-parents`, `skip`, `provide-input`) only when the recovery is a distinct API — not `use-value` with a magic payload (PCL `skip-log-entry`).
- `handler-bind` to invoke restarts (stack live). `handler-case` only to unwind/translate. No `ignore-errors` / catch-all `error` in library code.
- `error` / `cerror` / `signal` / `warn` / `check-type` / `assert` — use the construct that already establishes the right restart (`cerror` → `continue`; `check-type`/`assert` → `store-value`).
- Typed `foo-error` tree + slots + `:report`. Protocol owns types; backends signal them. Wire codes are slots, not the handler key.
- Reuse well-known conditions (`usocket:*`, dexador errors, UIOP `parameter-error`, Alexandria `required-argument`). Wrap into protocol types if needed; keep `:cause`. `lparallel:task-handler-bind` across worker threads.

Skill: **cl-stack-conditions**.
